# Shared "Target unit / board" selection for the M5Unit-NFC UnitUnified examples (ESP-IDF).
# Used by the ViaPaHub example, which reaches the unit through an I2C multiplexer and therefore
# only works with units that sit on an external I2C port (UnitNFC, UnitRFID2).
# rsource'd from each example's main/Kconfig.projbuild. The chosen CONFIG_EXAMPLE_USING_* is mapped
# to the source-level USING_* macro in common/variant.cmake (shared with the Arduino build).
menu "M5Unit-NFC example"

choice EXAMPLE_NFC_VARIANT
    prompt "Target unit / board"
    default EXAMPLE_USING_UNIT_NFC
    help
        Which NFC/RFID unit this example drives through the PaHub.
        CapCC1101NFC is not listed because it is an SPI unit, and the M5Dial built-in WS1850S is not
        listed because it sits on the internal I2C bus; neither can be reached through a PaHub.

    config EXAMPLE_USING_UNIT_NFC
        bool "UnitNFC (ST25R3916, I2C / GROVE)"
    config EXAMPLE_USING_UNIT_RFID2
        bool "UnitRFID2 (WS1850S, I2C / GROVE)"
        help
            The Arduino build gets M5Unit-RFID from lib_deps, but an ESP-IDF native build does not:
            this example's idf_component.yml names only the libraries of the repository it sits in.
            An ESP-IDF native build of M5Unit-NFC's copy therefore cannot build this variant; use
            M5Unit-RFID's copy.
endchoice

endmenu
